// Rule: [T1649] Certighost - AD CS Chase to Non DC
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1649
// Classification: Validation query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR
// Required telemetry: DeviceNetworkEvents
// Purpose: Validation query for ad cs chase to non dc, with evidence boundaries and target-environment validation requirements
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceNetworkEvents for ad cs chase to non dc using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result shows source-observed CA egress to LDAP or SMB/LSA toward an address that is absent from the approved DC inventory.
// A match does not prove: successful certificate issuance, PKINIT, DCSync, or CVE-2026-54121 abuse.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Certighost AD CS chase to a non-Domain-Controller destination
// Classification: Validation query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Platform: Microsoft Defender XDR Advanced Hunting
// Required telemetry: DeviceNetworkEvents from every Enterprise CA host
//
// Replace the environment-specific values before execution. The CA and
// Domain Controller inventories are required controls, not optional tuning.
let EnterpriseCAHosts = dynamic(["<CA_FQDN>"]);
let ApprovedDomainControllerIPs = dynamic(["<DC_IP_1>", "<DC_IP_2>"]);
DeviceNetworkEvents
| where DeviceName in~ (EnterpriseCAHosts)
| where RemotePort in (389, 445)
| where RemoteIP !in (ApprovedDomainControllerIPs)
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceId,
    DeviceName,
    RemoteIP,
    RemotePort,
    RemoteUrl,
    Protocol,
    ActionType,
    InitiatingProcessFileName,
    InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    ReportId

// Interpretation:
// A result shows source-observed CA egress to LDAP or SMB/LSA toward an
// address that is absent from the approved DC inventory. It does not prove
// successful certificate issuance, PKINIT, DCSync, or CVE-2026-54121 abuse.
//
// Promote only after validating inventory completeness, sensor coverage,
// legitimate CA-to-member-server traffic, and corroborating CA/Kerberos logs.
